    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #295\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPush succeeded. Working tree is clean, nothing left to commit.\n\nBranch: `bb/relay-269-review-debt-04-12-type-the-imap-flag-w-thr_quh8t2vs8r`\n\n## Summary\n\nAddressed all findings from the earlier AI code review on PR #295 for issue #269:\n\n- **`imapReconcile.ts`**: `ImapMailClient.setMessageFlag`'s `flag` parameter is now typed as `WritableImapFlag` (a union of the two canonical constants `IMAP_SEEN_FLAG`/`IMAP_FLAGGED_FLAG` from `messageFlags.ts`), which are now imported directly alongside a new exported `WRITABLE_IMAP_FLAGS` enumerable form.\n- **`imapFlowClient.ts`**: the real `ImapFlowMailClient.setMessageFlag` implementation matches the narrowed type.\n- **`mailSync.test.ts`**: added a compile-time-only `@ts-expect-error` guard (inside a declared-but-never-invoked function) asserting `setMessageFlag` rejects a non-canonical flag like `\\Deleted` — verified this actually catches a regression by temporarily widening the type to `string` and confirming `tsc` then flags the directive as unused.\n- **`mailboxClientViewType.ts`**: replaced the `\"read\"`/`\"flagged\"` magic-string Zod schema defaults with `READ_PROPERTY_KEY`/`FLAGGED_PROPERTY_KEY` imported from `messageFlags.ts`; runtime defaults unchanged.\n- **`mailboxClientView.test.ts`**: added tests confirming the schema still parses to `\"read\"`/`\"flagged\"` when those keys are omitted.\n- **`messageFlags.ts`**: reordered `WritableImapFlag`'s declaration above `MESSAGE_FLAG_PROPERTIES` for top-to-bottom readability.\n\nAlso merged in `develop`'s concurrent changes (unrelated inbox-pipeline/journal work) that had landed on the remote branch, resolved automatically with no conflicts.\n\nVerified after the merge: `pnpm -r run build` (backend, all packages) clean; `vitest run` — **26 test files, 333 tests, all passed**; `web`: `tsc --noEmit` clean.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
